Feature: slice-6 / playwright-e2e-both-locales
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-6
Verified: 2026-05-28

What was built
==============
Playwright now runs every spec under tests/e2e/ twice — once under
Polish browser locale + Accept-Language, once under English — so the
launch suite catches per-locale regressions before they ship.

Mechanism (the standard Playwright pattern):
- playwright.config.ts declares two projects: `chromium-pl`
  (locale "pl-PL", Accept-Language pl-PL,pl;q=0.9) and
  `chromium-en` (locale "en-GB", Accept-Language en-GB,en;q=0.9).
  Browser locale drives navigator.languages; next-intl's
  "as-needed" routing serves PL on bare paths and EN under /en
  when the request says so.
- A tiny dispatcher at tests/e2e/_locales.ts lets specs pick
  text + URL via:
    forLocale({ pl: "Załóż konto", en: "Create account" })
    urlPrefix()  →  "" for PL, "/en" for EN
- register-therapist.spec.ts refactored to use these helpers.
  Heading text, submit-button name, route, and the verify-email
  redirect target all branch per locale.

Coverage
========
2 specs × 2 locales = 4 tests today:
  [chromium-pl] therapist email form: validates + fires CreateUser
  [chromium-pl] /login redirects cross-origin
  [chromium-en] therapist email form: validates + fires CreateUser
  [chromium-en] /login redirects cross-origin

All 4 pass against a clean dev server.

Adding a new spec — no per-locale duplication needed. New tests use
the dispatcher and automatically fan out across both projects
because Playwright copies the spec into every project's run.

